--|---|\\n| NHA exact match | 195 | VeNom term already exists in Mondo non-human animal branch |\\n| Human analog found | 991 | No NHA term, but matching human/general disease exists |\\n| No match | 4,085 | No name/synonym match in Mondo |\\n\\n- 174 unique Mondo NHA terms matched (some have multiple VeNom xrefs due to VeNom duplicates/variants)\\n- 16 false positives identified and reclassified, including:\\n  - Subtype concepts that over-matched to generic parents (e.g., \\\"Cachexia - cancer\\\" ≠ cancer)\\n  - Clinical severity grades that are distinct from the base concept (PLE CCECAI scores)\\n  - Concepts that matched via synonym but are different diseases (e.g., \\\"Cataract - Morgagnian\\\" ≠ CPAMD8-related cataract)\\n  - Concepts where the VeNom term is a synonym but not an exact match (e.g., \\\"Spiking mortality syndrome\\\" ≠ poult enteritis mortality syndrome; \\\"Osteochondrosis (Juvenile osteochondritis, dyschondroplasia)\\\" has additional scope)\\n\\n### Phase 3: Three separate ROBOT templates\\n\\n#### Template 1: NHA exact matches — add xrefs and synonyms (complete)\\n- File: `data/ROBOT_add_venom_xrefs_nha_matches.tsv`...\n  Line 62:       \"body\": \"Updated NHA exact matches to 231. \\n\\nPlan to proceed with venom alignment and address exact synonyms later because this requires a plan to: \\n\\n- name each exact synonym with a non-human animal specific name, or\\n- allow the same exact synonyms to be present in the human and NHA branches (e.g., hemophilia B, non human animal\\\" and \\\"hemophilia B\\\" would have the same exact synonym factor IX deficiency. \\n- Consider human and non-human subsets to accomplish this and allowing the same exact synonyms across the two subsets but not within each subset or a source annotation on NHA exact synonyms that would be MONDO:NonHumanAnimalDisease, or the like.\",\n\n  Line 77:       \"body\": \"Updated implementation plan up to template 1:\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Data source\\n- VeNom 