 terms via cross-species analog pattern (v2 → curated v2)\\n- Original file: `data/ROBOT_add_venom_xrefs_human_analogs.tsv` (587 rows)\\n- Intermediate file: `data/ROBOT_add_venom_xrefs_human_analogs_v2.tsv` (811 data rows)\\n- Curated source of truth: `data/curated_ROBOT_add_venom_xrefs_human_analogs_v2.tsv` (**728 data rows**)\\n- Creates new NHA terms with cross-species analog matches\\n- New terms follow `nonhuman_disease.yaml` pattern: \\\"{human disease}, non-human animal\\\"\\n- Definition: \\\"{human disease} that occurs in non-human animals.\\\" with xref `MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease`\\n- Logical definition: `EquivalentTo MONDO:0005583 and (MONDO:0700097 some {human analog})`\\n- Each gets: VeNom xref (`MONDO:equivalentTo`), VeNom name as synonym where it differs, abbreviation synonyms\\n- Includes `in_subset` annotations (6 animal type subsets) and `term_tracker_item`\\n- New MONDO IDs: MONDO:1013000 – MONDO:1013793\\n- v2 changes:\\n  - 40 rows removed (moved to Template 1 — NHA terms already existed)\\n  - 166 rows added from the 404 no-match file — valid single-word exact matches that were incorrectly excluded by the original matching (e.g., \\\"Acne\\\" → acne, \\\"Botulism\\\" → botulism, \\\"Rabies\\\" → rabies, \\\"Tetanus\\\" → tetanus)\\n  - 67 rows added from Template 3 candidates — \\\"unspecified\\\" qualifier terms that map directly to the base disease human analog (e.g., \\\"Gastritis (unspecified)\\\" → gastritis, \\\"Cholesteatoma (site unspecified)\\\" → cholesteatoma). These are not subtypes — the \\\"(unspecified)\\\" qualifier means the VeNom term IS the base disease.\\n  - 9 human analog corrections (e.g., \\\"familial hyperlipidemia\\\" → \\\"hyperlipidemia\\\", \\\"adult teratoma\\\" → \\\"teratoma\\\", \\\"skin neoplasm\\\" → \\\"abscess\\\" for Abscess-skin)\\n  - 1 additional correction: \\\"Nephroblastoma (site unspecified)\\\" now maps to MONDO:0006058 \\\"Wilms tumor\\\" (generic) instead of MONDO:0008679 \\\"Wilms tumor 1\